# OpenWolf - per-session state and generated scaffolding stay untracked; the
# durable knowledge files are tracked. `openwolf update` preserves those as user
# data (USER_DATA_FILES in the CLI's update.js); everything else under .wolf/ is
# regenerated by `openwolf init --agent claude` in a fresh clone, so tracking it
# only churns on every upgrade and invites local edits the next update strips.
# Allowlist, not a blocklist, so a new OpenWolf artefact is ignored by default.
# Same rule in every repo under ~/Projects.
.wolf/*
!.wolf/cerebrum.md
!.wolf/STATUS.md
!.wolf/config.json
!.wolf/buglog.json

# Local tooling scratch, not part of the project.
.gastown-ignore
__pycache__/

# Screenshot sources. The README serves the .webp beside them, converted with
# `cwebp -resize 900 0 -q 80 -m 6 shot.png -o shot.webp`. The PNGs are ~1-2MB
# each and would only ever be duplicates in the history.
docs/screenshots/*.png

.claude/rules/openwolf.md
.claude/settings.json
.claude/commands/designqc.md
.claude/commands/reframe.md
.claude/commands/security-audit.md
.claude/skills/designqc/
.claude/skills/reframe/
.codex/
.opencode/
AGENTS.md
